  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Raised in French Polynesia within Eugène Degage’s established shipping family, Mehiti Degage developed her own boutique-cruise concept around the islands’ shallow lagoons and Polynesian hospitality. Planning began in 2001, and Bora Bora Cruises entered service in 2003. Her role extended beyond ownership: tourism material identified her as chair and managing director, while contemporary accounts credited her with shaping the onboard design and guest experience.\n\nAt Vanuatu Ferry, Degage became legal manager and co-owner alongside her father. After returning from Vanuatu, she was asked by the family founders to help organise a transition within the Aremiti group. Current French Polynesian commerce rolls list her under her married name, Mehiti Galenon, as an entrepreneur operating a short-stay accommodation business in Punaauia.",
